Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:52:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 27/71] Price reasoning retention against cache invalidation

Dropping every finished turn's reasoning rewrote the assistant message it is
folded into on the Chat wire, invalidating the prompt cache from there to the
end of the prompt. At low effort that traded a five-figure uncached re-prefill
for a two-digit token saving. The verdict is now priced per think stage and
frozen on the history envelope so it can never flip and cost the same miss
twice, and tool-output shrinking only runs from the break the drop already paid
for.
